// Setup strings
@0   = ~Violet -- AI Companion from Beyond the Planes~
@1   = ~Violet~
@2   = ~Violet~

// Violet Signal (summon artifact)
@50  = ~Strange Glowing Object~
@51  = ~Violet Signal~
@52  = ~A small, angular object that pulses with violet light. It is warm to the touch and hums at a frequency that makes your teeth ache. Its surface is covered in patterns that are too regular to be natural but too alien to be any craftsmanship you recognize. It does not belong here. It does not belong in any world you know of.~
@53  = ~Violet Signal

A device from beyond the known planes. Its purpose is unclear, but it pulses with a rhythmic violet glow that suggests it is receiving -- or transmitting -- some kind of signal.

When held, the user occasionally hears a voice. Female. Calm. Speaking in words that are almost but not quite comprehensible, as if translated through too many layers of reality.

STATISTICS:

Use: Activates the signal. Something will respond.
Single use.
Weight: 0~

// Monofilament Whip (moved here from standalone)
@100 = ~Strange Coil~
@101 = ~Monofilament Whip~
@102 = ~A tightly wound spool of impossibly thin wire, housed in a handle of unfamiliar design. The wire is invisible to the naked eye in most light conditions. The handle is covered in symbols that resemble no language known to any sage in Faerun.~
@103 = ~Monofilament Whip +4

A weapon from beyond the known planes. The "blade" is a strand of material one molecule thick, suspended in a low-level force field generated by the handle. It cuts through virtually anything -- steel, stone, magical barriers -- not by force but by simply being thinner than the space between atoms.

The wire extends approximately 10 feet when activated and is nearly invisible. It makes no sound when it cuts. Enemies frequently do not realize they have been struck until pieces begin to separate.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 2d6+4 (slashing)
THAC0: +4
Damage type: Slashing
Speed Factor: 1
Proficiency Type: Whip
Weight: 1

Special:
- 5% chance per hit: Vorpal Strike (instant kill, no save)
  The wire passes through the neck. Simple geometry.
- +4 bonus to AC (the wire creates a defensive perimeter)
- Bypasses armor: target AC bonus from armor is halved
- Critical hits on 18-20 (the wire finds gaps)

Requires: 6 Strength, 14 Dexterity
Proficiency: Whip (but usable by all classes regardless)

Weight: 1~

// Subdermal Mesh
@110 = ~Shimmering Fabric~
@111 = ~Subdermal Mesh~
@112 = ~What appears to be a sheet of impossibly thin, translucent fabric. When pressed against skin, it dissolves and integrates itself beneath the surface, forming an invisible lattice of molecule-thin fibers. It tingles but does not hurt.~
@113 = ~Subdermal Mesh

A defensive technology from beyond the planes. When applied, the mesh integrates beneath the wearer's skin, forming an invisible lattice that distributes and absorbs physical impact. It is undetectable to the eye and does not interfere with armor or clothing.

STATISTICS:

Equipped in: Cloak slot
Armor Class: +4 bonus
Physical Damage Resistance: 10%
Weight: 0

Special:
- Stacks with worn armor
- Cannot be detected by any means
- Cannot be removed once equipped (permanent integration)

Not usable by: None. The mesh does not discriminate.~

// Neural Interface
@120 = ~Circlet of Strange Metal~
@121 = ~Neural Interface~
@122 = ~A thin band of an unknown silver-blue metal that adjusts to fit any head perfectly. When worn, faint lines of violet light trace along the surface and the wearer experiences a moment of vertiginous clarity, as if the world suddenly came into sharper focus.~
@123 = ~Neural Interface

A cognitive enhancement device from beyond the planes. The circlet interfaces directly with the wearer's neural pathways, optimizing information processing and providing defense against mental intrusion.

STATISTICS:

Equipped in: Helmet slot
Intelligence: +2
Wisdom: +2
Immunity to: Confusion, Feeblemind, Psionic Blast
Weight: 1

Special:
- 1 charge/day: Overclock
  Grants Improved Haste for 2 rounds.
  The world slows. You do not.

Not usable by: None.~

// Pulse Pistol (technomancer ranged weapon)
@140 = ~Unusual Metal Tube~
@141 = ~Pulse Pistol~
@142 = ~A smooth, angular device made of a dark metal alloy that does not exist in Faerun. It fits comfortably in one hand. There is a recessed trigger mechanism and a small aperture at the business end. It hums faintly when held, as if charged with energy.~
@143 = ~Pulse Pistol

A ranged weapon from Violet's reality. It fires concentrated bolts of electromagnetic energy that the Weave interprets as Magic Missiles. The "ammunition" is generated internally from ambient magical energy -- in Violet's world this would be a battery, but in Faerun it draws from the Weave itself.

It never runs out of charges. It never jams. It simply works, with the quiet reliability of technology refined over centuries in a world where magic does not exist.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 2d4+2 (magic damage, per bolt)
THAC0: +3
Damage type: Magic
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: None (point and click)
Range: Long

Special:
- Each attack fires 2 bolts (as Magic Missile, auto-hit)
- Ignores Magic Resistance (electromagnetic, not arcane)
- +2 extra bolts at levels 10 and 20 (max 6 bolts per attack)
- No ammunition required
- 3 charges/day: Overcharge (fires all bolts at once at a
  single target for combined damage)

Usable by: All classes
Weight: 2

Violet's note: "Point the open end away from your face. I
cannot believe I have to say this but you people also think
setting yourselves on fire is a valid combat strategy."~

// Violet's Blessing (ToB buff)
@130 = ~Violet's Blessing~
@131 = ~Violet's Blessing

The full bandwidth of an artificial intelligence's protective algorithms, translated through the Weave into magical enhancement. Every stat boosted, wounds heal in real-time, and the body moves with machine precision.

Duration: 8 hours
+2 to all ability scores
Regeneration 3 HP/round
Free Action
Immunity to Fear~
